HALF NORMAL+SIMPLE POLINOMIAL
HALF NORMALWITHOUT ADJUSTMENT
HAZARD RATE WITHOUT ADJUSTMENT
HAZARD RATE+ SIMPLE POLINOMIAL
HAZARD RATE +HERMITE POLINOMIAL
To compare between models, used Akaike criteria (AIC y Delta AIC)(Akaike 1974);  Q-Q Plots and asocciated test Kolmorov-Smirnov y Cramer-Von Mises.
Models presented no important differences between them in estimated D, DCV, AIC, and Delta AC. Then I analized the Q-Q Plots and goodness of fit asocciated test Kolmorov-Smirnov y Cramer-Von Mises of each one and all the models seems to show a good concordance between the models and my data. I finally selected the HAZARD RATE WITHOUT ADJUSTMENT.

Ok, one problem that i have with the results, and that seems not ok, is that the confidence interval obtained for N, is between 0 and 1000 individuals, and the estimated N is of 1000. This looks like no logical, so I think that my analisis may be wrong, but if that it is the case, why all the models adjust well?

